<title>GERMANY: EU 1997 oilseed area forecast rises to 5.70 mln ha.</title>
<headline>EU 1997 oilseed area forecast rises to 5.70 mln ha.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union oilseeds plantings for food and industrial use are seen rising to by 4.6 percent to 5.70 million hectares in 1997, a statement from the grain trade lobby Coceral, received here, said.</p>
<p>The figure was up from a 5.54 million ha estimate made on April 11 by the EU oilseeds, animal fats and vegetable oils association ANGO, which has since joined Coceral.</p>
<p>The Brussels-based organisations drew on its own figures as well as those obtained from German grain trader Toepfer.</p>
<p>Overall rapeseed plantings are expected to rise by 6.7 percent to 2.82 million ha and sunflowerseed plantings to increase by 0.1 percent to 2.48 million ha.</p>
<p>Soybean plantings were put at 405,000 ha, up 21.6 percent.</p>
<p>The figure compared the 1997 forecast with revised 1996 data and did not include minor seeds such as linseed.</p>
<p>    EU Oilseed Area     1997 pct change 1996  April 97 forecast</p>
<p>    (million ha)						    for 1997</p>
<p>    Rapeseed		2.821  +  6.7   2.644     2.687</p>
<p>    Of which industrial 0.332  - 41.1   0.564     0.329</p>
<p>    Sunflower seed	2.478  +  0.1   2.475     2.440</p>
<p>    Of which industrial 0.063  - 29.0   0.089     0.101</p>
<p>    Soybeans		0.405  + 21.6   0.333     0.417</p>
<p>(industrial - nil)</p>
<p>    TOTAL OILSEEDS	5.704  +  4.6   5.452     5.544</p>
<p>    Of which industrial 0.395  - 39.4   0.653     0.432</p>
<p>--Vera Eckert, Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
